// KNOWN SILENT-WRONG (open) — the monomorphization corner's SECOND face.
// NOT gated: this file documents a bug the medium does not yet catch. It
// compiles clean (zero diagnostics) and runs to the WRONG answer.
//
// The sibling repro (mn-unannotated-float-accumulator.mn) shows the corner via
// an unannotated RECURSIVE accumulator. This shows the SAME root via a NAMED
// GENERIC function applied HIGHER-ORDER — and it corrects an earlier scope claim
// (commit 24ce6462) that "the prelude combinators handle floats; only named
// recursion floors." That is INCOMPLETE: `sort` IS a prelude combinator and it
// does NOT sort floats, because it rests on `merge`, a named generic recursive
// fn; and `reduce(xs, min)` misorders because `min`/`max` are named generics.
//
// The ROOT (one root, three surfaces):
//   A named generic function (`min`, `max`, `merge`) has UNANNOTATED params, so
//   inference leaves its element type a variable and the fn compiles ONCE at the
//   RI32 floor. Reached through the higher-order fn table (as a reducer value, or
//   recursively inside `sort`), it receives the word-protocol REFERENCES to the
//   f64 values and compares them as i32 (the reference addresses), never the
//   values. The values survive (the references are valid f64 cells), but the
//   ORDER is arbitrary — so `sort` returns its input unsorted and `reduce(xs,min)`
//   returns the wrong element. Silent: exit 1, never 42, no diagnostic.
//
// The WORKING forms — proven in tests/frontier/stats + the fixtures below:
//   - INLINE LAMBDA reducer: reduce(xs, (a,b) => if a<=b {a} else {b}) — the
//     lambda is specialized per call site at f64, so it is sound.
//   - ANNOTATED recursive helper (best_v: Float) — the CFC / stats-demo pattern;
//     the annotation monomorphizes the body to f64.
//   - map / filter / fold / each / reverse — all lambda-based, all sound.
//
// The ULTIMATE is whole-program monomorphization (Hβ.value.seq-element-stride-
// carrier, scalar half): emit min_i32 for Int call sites and min_f64 for Float
// ones and dispatch per site. The stride carrier (7db29195) fixed the SEQUENCE
// read (a generic body reading a packed [Float] reads its element stride live);
// this scalar half — a generic fn value compiled once — is the remaining work.
// A refusal-at-the-mismatch is a STOPGAP monomorphization deletes.
//
// Surfaced 2026-07-22 by the float-statistics validator (a named `min`/`max`/
// `sort` reducer diverged from numpy). Turn into a frontier gate (expecting 42,
// or a run_refusal) when the keystone lands.

fn main() = {
  let xs = [3.5, 1.5, 2.5, 0.5, 4.5]
  // reduce with the NAMED generic min: expect 0.5, gets a wrong element
  let rmin = reduce(xs, min)
  // sort over floats: expect [0.5, 1.5, 2.5, 3.5, 4.5], returns xs unsorted
  let smallest = sort(xs)[0]
  // the WORKING inline-lambda form, for contrast (this half is sound)
  let lmin = reduce(xs, (a, b) => if a <= b { a } else { b })
  if rmin == 0.5 && smallest == 0.5 && lmin == 0.5 { 42 } else { 1 }
}
